<title>UK: Wickes firms after narrower losses.</title>
<headline>Wickes firms after narrower losses.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in home improvement chain Wickes Plc bucked a market downtrend, firming 1-1/2 pence to 153 after the group trimmed its 1996 losses.</p>
<p>Upbeat comments on the 1997 outlook also helped the shares, market makers said.</p>
<p>Wickes, haunted by an accounting scandal last year, said it made a staisfactory start of 1997 after 1996 pre-tax losses shrank to 55.7 million stg from 279.30 million the previous year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
